---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
import DocsSidebar from "../../components/DocsSidebar.astro";

const usageCode = [
  `<span class="kw">import</span> { G2WGame } <span class="kw">from</span> <span class="str">"@g2w/runtime"</span>;`,
  `<span class="kw">import</span> { PixiRenderer } <span class="kw">from</span> <span class="str">"@g2w/renderer-pixi"</span>;`,
  ``,
  `<span class="kw">const</span> game = <span class="kw">new</span> <span class="type">G2WGame</span>({`,
  `  renderer: <span class="kw">new</span> <span class="type">PixiRenderer</span>(),`,
  `  canvas: document.<span class="fn">querySelector</span>(<span class="str">"#game"</span>)!,`,
  `  width: <span class="num">640</span>, height: <span class="num">360</span>,`,
  `  <span class="fn">onUpdate</span>: (deltaTime) => { <span class="cm">/* your game logic here */</span> },`,
  `});`,
  ``,
  `<span class="kw">await</span> game.<span class="fn">init</span>();`,
  `game.<span class="fn">start</span>();`,
].join("\n");
---

<Base title="Introduction · g2w docs">
  <div class="docs">
    <DocsSidebar active="introduction" />

    <main class="docs-main prose">
      <div class="crumb">docs / getting-started / introduction</div>
      <h1>Introduction</h1>
      <p>
        <b>g2w (Game to Website)</b> is a TypeScript-first, AI-agent-ready framework for
        building and shipping web games: HTML5 games, 2D first with 3D planned, for
        desktop and mobile web browsers.
      </p>
      <p>
        A game in g2w is a composition of small packages. You build a
        <code>G2WGame</code> from <code>@g2w/runtime</code> with a renderer, a
        <code>SceneManager</code>, input adapters, audio, and assets — then register your
        resources as finalizers and let the Effect runtime own the lifecycle.
      </p>

      <h2 id="lifecycle">Lifecycle states</h2>
      <p>
        <code>Game</code> owns an explicit lifecycle state machine:
        <code>new → initializing → initialized → running ⇄ stopped → disposed</code>. A
        failed init returns to <code>new</code> and is retryable; disposal is idempotent
        and every cleanup failure stays observable.
      </p>

      <h2 id="usage">Minimal usage</h2>
      <div class="codeblock" style="box-shadow: none">
        <div class="cb-head"><span>main.ts</span></div>
        <pre><code set:html={usageCode} /></pre>
      </div>

      <h2>Honest status</h2>
      <div class="callout" style="box-shadow: none">
        <span class="tag">Status</span>
        <span>
          <b>The @g2w/* packages are on npm at 0.1.0</b> (released 2026-10-28) — an
          early 0.x release, so the public API may still change before 1.0.
          2D rendering over WebGL is done and browser-verified; 3D is exploratory
          (Roadmap R8).
        </span>
      </div>

      <h2 id="next">Next steps</h2>
      <p>
        Read the <a href="https://github.com/AlexanderDev2004/g2w/blob/main/docs/architecture.md"
          >architecture notes</a
        > for the implemented design, or the
        <a href="https://github.com/AlexanderDev2004/g2w/blob/main/ROADMAP.md">roadmap</a>
        for current priorities and planned work.
      </p>
    </main>

    <aside class="docs-toc">
      <div class="ttl">On this page</div>
      <a class="on" href="#">Introduction</a>
      <a href="#lifecycle">Lifecycle states</a>
      <a href="#usage">Minimal usage</a>
      <a href="#next">Next steps</a>
    </aside>
  </div>
</Base>
